diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a9642fd
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+# Chat Bots Design Notes
+
+## Data Model (`User` + `User::Bot`)
+
+Bots are represented in the `users` table with `role: :bot` (`enum :role, %i[ member administrator bot ]`):
+
+- **`creator_id`**: Foreign key to `users` (`belongs_to :creator, class_name: "User", optional: true`), recording which chat member created the bot. Because `User::Role#can_administer?` checks `administrator? || self == record&.creator`, creators and administrators automatically have permission to manage a bot while other regular members do not.
+- **`bot_token` & `bot_key`**: Active bots receive a unique 24-character `SecureRandom.base58` `bot_token` on creation. The externally visible bot code (`User#bot_key`) is `"#{id}-#{bot_token}"`. `User.authenticate_bot(bot_key)` looks up the active bot by primary key `id` and compares `bot_token` in constant time via `ActiveSupport::SecurityUtils.secure_compare`.
+- **`auto_join_open_rooms`**: Boolean (`default: false, null: false`), controlled by the `"Add to all open rooms"` switch on `/bots/new` and `/bots/:id/edit`.
+- **Deactivation (Deletion)**: Deleting a bot calls `User#deactivate`, which sets `status: :deactivated`, clears `bot_token: nil`, destroys its webhook, and removes non-direct room memberships while preserving historical messages authored by the bot.
+- **Room Memberships**:
+  - Human users join all open rooms by default (`User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms` and `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` via `User.open_room_grantees`).
+  - Bots do **not** join open rooms by default (`auto_join_open_rooms: false`). Room admins/creators can toggle individual bots on open rooms (`Rooms::OpensController` / `app/views/rooms/opens/`), closed rooms (`Rooms::ClosedsController`), and direct rooms (`Rooms::DirectsController`).
+  - When `auto_join_open_rooms` is switched on (`true`), the bot joins all existing open rooms (`after_save_commit :grant_membership_to_open_rooms`) and every open room created or converted from closed afterward (`User.open_room_grantees`). Turning `auto_join_open_rooms` off keeps the bot's current memberships.
+  - Human-only flows (`/account/edit` member list, `/session`, session transfers, IP bans) scope queries with `User.without_bots`.
+
+## Bot HTTP API (`Messages::ByBotsController`)
+
+- **Endpoint**: `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages` (`constraints: { room_id: /[^\/]+/, bot_key: /[^\/]+/ }`).
+- **Raw Body Handling**: `curl -d "..."` sends `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded` by default even though the payload is raw text (which may contain `%`, `+`, `&`, etc.). `Messages::ByBotsController` sets `wrap_parameters false` and `request.request_parameters = {}` in `process_action` before Rails instrumentation accesses `request.filtered_parameters`, preventing Rack/Rails form/JSON parameter parsers from raising `400 Bad Request` on raw bodies. The raw UTF-8 body is read from `request.raw_post`.
+- **Validation & Extension Point for Attachments**: `Message` validates `ensure_body_or_attachment_present` (`body.blank? && body.body&.attachables.blank? && !attachment?`). If future features add file attachment uploads for bots (e.g., binary bodies by `Content-Type` or `multipart/form-data`), `Messages::ByBotsController#create` can attach the file and call `@message.process_attachment` before `@message.broadcast_create`.
+- **Broadcasts & Push Notifications**: Setting `Current.user = bot` sets `message.creator = bot`. Saving triggers `Room#receive` (`unread_memberships` + `Room::PushMessageJob`), and `@message.broadcast_create` appends the message via Turbo Streams and notifies `UnreadRoomsChannel`.
+
+## Bot Webhooks (`Webhook` + `Webhook::DeliveryJob`)
+
+- **Data Model**: `Webhook` (`webhooks` table with `user_id` foreign key and `url`) belongs to `User` (`has_one :webhook, dependent: :destroy, autosave: true` in `User::Bot`). `User::Bot` exposes `webhook_url` and `webhook_url=` so bot forms (`/bots/new` and `/bots/:id/edit`) can create, update, or clear a bot's webhook (saving an empty `webhook_url` destroys the `Webhook` record; `User#deactivate` also destroys it).
+- **URL Policy**: Validates `URI::HTTP` (`http`/`https`) with a present host, allowing self-hosted/internal/localhost endpoints without requiring external DNS resolution.
+- **`joined` Event**:
+  - `Membership.grant_for` uses `insert_all(..., returning: %i[ room_id user_id ])` (and `Membership` also defines `after_create_commit :deliver_joined_webhook_later` for single-record `create`), ensuring `Webhook::DeliveryJob` is enqueued after transaction commit (`ActiveRecord.after_all_transactions_commit`) **strictly for newly inserted memberships** of active bots with webhooks in non-direct rooms (`Room.without_directs`).
+  - Direct conversations (`Rooms::Direct`) never trigger `joined`.
+  - Posts `Content-Type: application/json` with `{ event: "joined", room: { id, name, reply_to } }`.
+- **`mention` Event**:
+  - Active bots in a room appear in `Autocompletable::UsersController` alongside human members and use standard ActionText `User` attachables (`User::Mentionable`). On `Message` creation, `Room#receive` calls `deliver_webhooks_later`, which enqueues a `Webhook::DeliveryJob` per active bot with a webhook in `message.mentionees` (ignoring bot-authored messages to prevent bot loops, and never blocking the HTTP request of the user posting the message).
+  - Posts `Content-Type: application/json` with `{ event: "mention", author, room: { id, name, reply_to }, message: { id, body: { text, html }, link } }`. `Message::Mentionee#plain_text_without_mention(bot)` strips only that bot's own `<action-text-attachment>` nodes from the rich-text fragment while preserving other mentions and `message.body.html`.
+- **Synchronous vs. Asynchronous Replies (for both `joined` and `mention`)**:
+  - `200` with `Content-Type: text/plain` escapes HTML entities and converts newlines to `<br>`, posting and broadcasting the message as the bot.
+  - `200` with `Content-Type: text/html` posts and broadcasts rich-text HTML (sanitized by ActionText and `ContentFilters`) as the bot.
+  - `204` (or non-text/non-200 responses) posts nothing synchronously; the bot can post asynchronously at any time via `room.reply_to` (`/rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages`).
+
+## Per-Member Bot Cap (`Account#settings.bots_per_member`)
+
+- **Account Setting**: `Account` defines `has_json :settings, restrict_room_creation_to_administrators: false, bots_per_member: 5` (validated to be a non-negative integer `>= 0`). Administrators configure `"Bots per member"` on `/account/edit`; non-administrators do not see or edit account settings.
+- **Limit Calculation (`User#reached_bot_limit?`)**:
+  - Administrators are never limited (`return false if administrator?`).
+  - For regular members, counts only active bots (`bots.active.count >= account.settings.bots_per_member`); deactivated (`deleted`) bots do not count.
+- **Enforcement & UI**:
+  - On `/bots` (`app/views/bots/index.html.erb`), when `Current.user.reached_bot_limit?` is true, the `"Add a chat bot"` link is omitted and replaced with a notice telling the member they have `"reached the limit"`.
+  - `BotsController` enforces `before_action :ensure_within_bot_limit, only: %i[ new create ]` (`head :forbidden`), and `User::Bot` validates `ensure_within_bot_limit` `on: :create, if: :bot?`.
+  - Lowering `bots_per_member` never removes or deactivates existing bots, and existing bots can still be edited or deleted while a member is at or above the limit.
+
+## Misbehaving Bot Protection & Suspension (`User::Bot::Suspendable` + `Bots::SuspensionsController`)
+
+- **Fixed Thresholds (Code Constants in `User::Bot::Suspendable`)**:
+  - `FLOOD_MESSAGE_LIMIT = 10` within `FLOOD_WINDOW = 10.seconds`.
+  - `COOLDOWN_DURATION = 30.seconds`, `COOLDOWN_SUSPENSION_ATTEMPTS = 5`.
+  - `WEBHOOK_FAILURE_LIMIT = 10` consecutive failed deliveries.
+- **Database-Backed State**: Stored on `users` (`suspended_at`, `suspension_reason`, `bot_cooldown_until`, `bot_cooldown_attempts`, `bot_post_timestamps`, `bot_webhook_failures`) and updated under `with_lock` so web workers (`Messages::ByBotsController`) and background workers (`Webhook::DeliveryJob`) coordinate atomically across processes without touching `updated_at` on routine message deliveries.
+- **Flooding & Cooldown**:
+  - Both `Messages::ByBotsController#create` and synchronous `Webhook#post_reply` route message posting through `User#deliver_bot_message`.
+  - Up to 10 messages in any sliding 10-second window are posted. The 11th message within 10 seconds is rejected and starts a 30-second cooldown (`bot_cooldown_until = now + 30.seconds`, `bot_cooldown_attempts = 0`).
+  - During the cooldown, `POST /rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages` responds `429 Too Many Requests` with `Retry-After` (remaining seconds), and synchronous webhook replies are suppressed.
+  - Five additional attempts during the same cooldown suspend the bot (`reason: "Flooding (too many messages)"`). If the cooldown expires first, `bot_cooldown_attempts` resets on any future cooldown.
+- **Failing Webhooks**:
+  - `Webhook#deliver_payload` treats any `2xx` (`Net::HTTPSuccess`) as a successful delivery (resetting `bot_webhook_failures` to `0`) and any non-`2xx` status, timeout, or connection/protocol exception as a failed delivery.
+  - Ten consecutive failed deliveries suspend the bot (`reason: "Failing webhooks (10 failed deliveries)"`).
+- **Suspended Bot Behavior & Reactivation**:
+  - Keeping `status: :active` while setting `suspended_at` / `suspension_reason` ensures suspended bots retain all rooms and messages, remain editable/deletable, stay listed on `/bots` as `"Suspended"` with their reason, and continue counting towards `Account#settings.bots_per_member`.
+  - Suspended bots receive `403 Forbidden` from `Messages::ByBotsController` and receive no `joined` or `mention` webhooks (`User.unsuspended` scopes in `Room` and `Membership`, plus `Webhook#active_recipient_in?`).
+  - Only administrators see the `"Reactivate"` button (with native `confirm()` via `data-turbo-confirm`) on `/bots` and are authorized for `DELETE /bots/:bot_id/suspension` (`Bots::SuspensionsController#destroy`), which calls `User#reactivate` to clear suspension, cooldown, flood window, and webhook failure counters.
